      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "NEW SHIPS, TIMELESS LEGACY \n\nThe Coast Guard is accelerating Waterways Commerce Cutter production with $162M in funding through the One Big Beautiful Bill Act. These modern ships will replace an aging fleet and keep America moving, maintaining 28,000+ aids to navigation and facilitating $5.4T in annual commerce. Designated as the “Chief Petty Officer Class,” these ships will proudly bear the names of Coast Guard Chief Petty Officers and honor their legacy as leaders, mentors, and technical experts. \n\n\"Since 1920, Chief Petty Officers and the Chiefs Mess have driven Coast Guard readiness and operational excellence,” said Master Chief Petty Officer of the Coast Guard Phillip Waldron. “These new cutters and their crews will build on that legacy, ensuring maritime commerce flows safely and we continue to control, secure and defend our inland ports and waterways and Marine Transportation System.”\n\nRead more here: https://t.co/j6him63eGC\n\n#uscg #forcedesign2028 @DHSgov",
      "text_resolved": "NEW SHIPS, TIMELESS LEGACY \n\nThe Coast Guard is accelerating Waterways Commerce Cutter production with $162M in funding through the One Big Beautiful Bill Act. These modern ships will replace an aging fleet and keep America moving, maintaining 28,000+ aids to navigation and facilitating $5.4T in annual commerce. Designated as the “Chief Petty Officer Class,” these ships will proudly bear the names of Coast Guard Chief Petty Officers and honor their legacy as leaders, mentors, and technical experts. \n\n\"Since 1920, Chief Petty Officers and the Chiefs Mess have driven Coast Guard readiness and operational excellence,” said Master Chief Petty Officer of the Coast Guard Phillip Waldron. “These new cutters and their crews will build on that legacy, ensuring maritime commerce flows safely and we continue to control, secure and defend our inland ports and waterways and Marine Transportation System.”\n\nRead more here: https://www.news.uscg.mil/Press-Releases/Article/4268624/us-coast-guard-announces-chief-petty-officer-class-for-new-waterways-commerce-c/\n\n#uscg #forcedesign2028 @DHSgov",
