      "reply_to_account_id": null,
      "quoted_tweet_id": null,
      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Yesterday, @USCG commissioned the Fast Response Cutter Earl Cunningham, honoring Boatswain’s Mate Second Class Earl Cunningham, who gave his life in 1936 during a heroic rescue on Lake Michigan.\n\nCunningham’s courage and legacy now inspire the mission of this cutter, which will strengthen our capabilities to defend Alaska’s maritime border and respond to crises. Through historic investment in the Coast Guard, we have ordered additional Fast Response Cutters.\n\nWelcome aboard, USCGC Earl Cunningham!  \n\nFollow @USCGArctic for more news about the Cunningham and its crew.\n\nRead more and hear from the CO here: https://t.co/WafGOBGJKe\n\n#uscg #ForceDesign2028 @DHSgov",
      "text_resolved": "Yesterday, @USCG commissioned the Fast Response Cutter Earl Cunningham, honoring Boatswain’s Mate Second Class Earl Cunningham, who gave his life in 1936 during a heroic rescue on Lake Michigan.\n\nCunningham’s courage and legacy now inspire the mission of this cutter, which will strengthen our capabilities to defend Alaska’s maritime border and respond to crises. Through historic investment in the Coast Guard, we have ordered additional Fast Response Cutters.\n\nWelcome aboard, USCGC Earl Cunningham!  \n\nFollow @USCGArctic for more news about the Cunningham and its crew.\n\nRead more and hear from the CO here: https://www.mycg.uscg.mil/News/Article/4271141/if-not-us-who-a-conversation-with-the-co-of-our-newest-fast-response-cutter/\n\n#uscg #ForceDesign2028 @DHSgov",
